""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-19T15:35:48-08:00","id":1005495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004230-donald-trump-in-the-wod?p=1005492#post1005492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say Narcissism, but that depends on what he would be willing to sacrifice for power, since the obsession with power to the loss of all else is what separates megalomania from narcissism, which is just being so self absorbed that nothing else matters, even power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is true. Trump's campaign always seemed like the man's experiment into how far he could take it. It just so happened that his first bid for presidency took him all the way to the white house. So it's less like he really wanted power, and more than he just wanted to inflate his own ego. His numerous social media and debate feuds with everyone from his fellow Republicans, to his opponent, to even the parents of a fallen US soldier only serve to validate that impression.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited"