ted ideas, stubborn, for sure; but willing to fight for what he believes in, and sacrifice everything if need be. Also King Arthur was a cannon Gurahl, so it's not like they haven't gotten political before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1043,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","user":"MrMarkers","date":". 12-04-2016, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1043-mrmarkers","name":"MrMarkers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1043_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T20:43:16-08:00","id":1012361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrMarkers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1004230-donald-trump-in-the-wod?p=1012346#post1012346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About perfect, if you've ever done any real research on the guys policies, or for the love he has for his nation, and ALL Americans. Go ahead and call me a right wing quack, but I'm a centrist libertarian, <b>the left went so far left</b> you all call me conservative now, and I believe you've been fooled into casting a man who loves his county into some despot.</div> </div> </div> </div>The American left is actually very centrist. The left of other nations is way farther to the left, generally. Europeans tend to find the notion of &quot;American left&quot; rather funny in this regard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If he's being cast as anything, it ought to be a good hearted man with some outdated ideas, stubborn, for sure; but willing to fight for what he believes in, and sacrifice everything if need be. Also King Arthur was a cannon Gurahl, so it's not like they haven't gotten political before </div> </div> </div>Locker room talk, supporting neo-nazis, being backed by neo-nazis, appointing a neo-nazi to lead strategist... we're not unfairly demonizing anyone, here. He's a reality TV host who didn't know what he was getting into, and now he's throwing stuff at the wall and seeing if it sticks. People elected him because of an image that was profoundly not him (an independent businessman who can enact good policies and eliminate corruption) when all evidence shows that he's an heir who avoids adversity, squanders his inheritance, requires the government to bail him out, and is in bed with everything he accused Hilarry of being in bed with on an order of magnitude that utterly dwarfs it, on top of his own personal sexual harassment issues.<br /> <br /> FOX News tried to spin some tale about his being like Quint in JAWS, but the thing is, Quint got eaten, and Peter Benchley wouldn't have written it the same way if he had been able to take another go at it.<br /> <br /> Well, he kind of did. You know the antagonist in that? A nazi sharkman. Weird, that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T21:10:02-08:00","id":1012369,"title":"","content":"Locker room talk:<br /> -Cause if you were in the public eye for 30+ years, you wouldn't say one thing you've regretted.<br /> <br /> supporting neo-nazis<br /> - citation needed <br /> <br /> being backed by neo-nazis<br /> - if 150,000 people supported anyone, some amount of them would be bigots of one shade or another. <br /> <br /> appointing a neo-nazi to lead strategist<br /> -you're kidding right? Calling Bannon a Nazi was just about as credible as calling Obama a Muslim.<br /> <br /> He's a reality TV host who didn't know what he was getting into, <br /> -Thats a weird way to say successful businessman that ran for president and won against all odds.<br /> <br /> and now he's throwing stuff at the wall and seeing if it sticks.<br /> -hes consistently had these policies since the 1980s, with the exception of abortion, and marijuana. But my guess is when you're 70 you'll have never changed your mind on anything.<br /> <br /> People elected him because of an image that was profoundly not him (an independent businessman who can enact good policies and eliminate corruption) when all evidence shows that he's an heir who avoids adversity, squanders his inheritance, requires the government to bail him out, and is in bed with everything he accused Hilarry of being in bed with on an order of magnitude that utterly dwarfs it.<br /> -HAHAHA oh wow, so you did like 0 reading on him other than huffpo, and watching CNN. I seriously have no idea how you could do any actual reading and not come to a conclusion that's not less biased than this. <br /> <br /> on top of his own personal sexual harassment issues.<br /> -While the jury is out on this, I think the issue should go there; you know to court, before it's bandied about with about with absolutely certainty. The fact is most of these charges had 0 proof, or were near immediately proven fraudulent.<br /> <br /> Edit: I won't be replying again because I don't want to get banned or 